CON-17: scale the full area and radius of custom ellipses with both axes

For HORIZ_ELLIPSE and VERT_ELLIPSE pipes without a size code,
xsect_setParams() set aFull = 1.2692*D^2 and rFull = 0.3061*D from the minor
axis D alone (the values of a standard 1:1.56 ellipse), while the width table
is scaled by the span. Area and width then describe different pipes, and the
change log at the top of this file already claims the fix for 5.3.0. Apply
the fix from origin/dev-elliptical_pipes (0c0a5ca3, with 8e27af6c keeping the
user's span): aFull = 0.8117*yFull*wMax, rFull = 0.2448*sqrt(yFull*wMax) for
both orientations. Both reduce to the old values for a 1:1.5636 ellipse.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-17_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/xsect.c b/src/legacy/engine/xsect.c
index cf40f97..a135be1 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/xsect.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/xsect.c
@@ -573,8 +573,8 @@ int xsect_setParams(TXsect *xsect, int type, double p[], double ucf)
             // --- length of major axis
             if ( p[1] < 0.0 ) return FALSE;
             xsect->wMax = p[1]/ucf;
-            xsect->aFull = 1.2692 * xsect->yFull * xsect->yFull;
-            xsect->rFull = 0.3061 * xsect->yFull;
+            xsect->aFull = 0.8117 * xsect->yFull * xsect->wMax;
+            xsect->rFull = 0.2448 * sqrt(xsect->yFull * xsect->wMax);
         }
         xsect->sFull = xsect->aFull * pow(xsect->rFull, 2./3.);
         xsect->sMax  = xsect->sFull;
@@ -601,8 +601,8 @@ int xsect_setParams(TXsect *xsect, int type, double p[], double ucf)
             // --- length of minor axis
             xsect->yFull = p[0]/ucf;
             xsect->wMax = p[1]/ucf;
-            xsect->aFull = 1.2692 * xsect->wMax * xsect->wMax;
-            xsect->rFull = 0.3061 * xsect->wMax;
+            xsect->aFull = 0.8117 * xsect->yFull * xsect->wMax;
+            xsect->rFull = 0.2448 * sqrt(xsect->yFull * xsect->wMax);
         }
         xsect->sFull = xsect->aFull * pow(xsect->rFull, 2./3.);
         xsect->sMax  = xsect->sFull;
